{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Eye to eye.</b> Concerning the glory that the elders saw, or concerning the appearance of the glory of YHWH before the eyes of the children of Israel — and this is the correct one." "<b>You appear.</b> Past tense; its sense is 'you appeared, YHWH,' and likewise 'and I remain,' and likewise 'for I am languishing' — because the lamed has a kamatz gadol." "<b>Stand over them.</b> When they sit."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:35.263164721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}